{
 "subject": "chess",
 "doc": "Prerequisite graph over the live curriculum's lessons (curriculum-build/chess/drafts/Cxx.txt, the source the app's CSV is built from). Each node is matched to lessons by a regex on the lesson TITLE; its position is its first lesson. An edge A -> B means A must be secure before B is introduced (research/03 section 2.4 chains, which are a synthesis [P/M], plus rules that are logically required). verify-skill-curricula.js checks every node matches a lesson and every edge is respected, and lists the lessons each node owns so the app can keep a per-node knowledge/skill state for adaptation. Stage = progression.json stage id where the node is first taught. Edges are only true prerequisites (B cannot be understood without A); a suggested teaching order is not an edge (e.g. grabbing a free, unprotected piece needs no piece values, so hanging pieces may come before points).",
